course: dictionary
lesson: 5707
title: Feelings in words: loneliness
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Loneliness is a noun. It is the sad feeling you have when you are alone, or when you feel that nobody cares about you or understands you. Look at the clue in this sentence: «Loneliness is feeling that nobody is with you.»
explain: You can feel lonely even when you are surrounded by people. «Three months into a new school, Zainab still ate lunch alone most days.» She was at school with other children, yet she felt alone. So loneliness is about how you feel, not only about where you are.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Zainab felt ___ at lunchtime.» If you put in "a sad feeling of being alone", the sentence still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Loneliness means the sad feeling of being alone, or of feeling that nobody cares about you or understands you.
fact: Loneliness can also mean being in a place far from other people, like «a far-away farm».
fact: «Loneliness» is a feeling that many people have, including other children, so it is nothing to be ashamed of.
fact: Clubs, teams, buddy benches, and keeping in touch with people far away can all help with loneliness.
fact: Talking to someone, joining in, or inviting others along can help when you feel lonely.
exercise: «Loneliness is feeling that nobody is with you.» What does loneliness mean? | A loud noise in a crowd | *The sad feeling of being alone | A happy time with many friends | A kind of school lunch
exercise: «Three months into a new school, Zainab still ate lunch alone most days.» What does this sentence show about loneliness? | Loneliness only happens to people who live far away | Loneliness means you like being quiet | *You can feel lonely even when you are with other people | Loneliness is a type of sports game
exercise: Which of these helps with loneliness, according to the examples? | Telling people they are "too loud" | Being picked last | *Joining a club or team | Shutting yourself in your room
test: «Loneliness has many shapes: a big brother who shuts his door at 13, friends who say you're "too loud", being picked last, a far-away farm.» What does the text say loneliness is rarely about? | Where you live | The weather | How old you are | *Something wrong with you
test: Which word means nearly the same as loneliness in the sentence «Loneliness is feeling that nobody is with you»? | Feeling excited | Feeling sleepy | Feeling hungry | *Feeling alone
exam: «Boredom is sometimes mixed with other feelings, like tiredness or loneliness, and naming the real feeling helps.» Why does the author say naming the real feeling helps? | Because loneliness and boredom are the same word | Because feelings never matter | *Because knowing the true feeling helps you deal with it | Because you should always say you are tired
